1
00:00:08,517 --> 00:00:11,892
This is Part 1 of 6: If
you think you understand.

2
00:00:12,710 --> 00:00:17,902
It comes from After Anatta: notes
by John Tan, known as Thusness.

3
00:00:17,982 --> 00:00:21,666
The six parts make one article,
called Dependent Arising:

4
00:00:21,746 --> 00:00:24,360
If You Think You Understand, You Don't.

5
00:00:25,262 --> 00:00:27,709
"If you think you understand
quantum mechanics,

6
00:00:27,789 --> 00:00:30,237
you don't understand quantum mechanics."

7
00:00:30,317 --> 00:00:32,913
Richard Feynman is said
to have quipped that.

8
00:00:32,993 --> 00:00:34,666
The same trap waits here.

9
00:00:34,746 --> 00:00:37,356
If you think you understand
dependent arising,

10
00:00:37,436 --> 00:00:39,928
you don't understand dependent arising.

11
00:00:40,737 --> 00:00:43,822
On paper it sounds
straightforward, even safe.

12
00:00:43,902 --> 00:00:45,593
When this is, that is.

13
00:00:45,682 --> 00:00:48,469
From the arising of this, that arises.

14
00:00:48,549 --> 00:00:50,697
When this is not, that is not.

15
00:00:50,777 --> 00:00:53,460
From the ceasing of this, that ceases.

16
00:00:53,576 --> 00:00:56,757
Things arise from many
causes and conditions,

17
00:00:56,837 --> 00:00:59,234
and nothing has an essence of its own.

18
00:01:00,037 --> 00:01:02,742
It reads like ordinary cause and effect.

19
00:01:02,822 --> 00:01:07,375
It fits easily onto the everyday,
objective picture of the world.

20
00:01:07,455 --> 00:01:09,359
But is it really that straightforward?

21
00:01:09,439 --> 00:01:12,529
Take two ordinary examples, and enquire.

22
00:01:13,350 --> 00:01:14,710
The first is an apple.

23
00:01:14,790 --> 00:01:19,493
When I toss an apple and catch it,
I feel I am handling one solid,

24
00:01:19,573 --> 00:01:23,719
independent object. It has
edges, weight and speed.

25
00:01:23,799 --> 00:01:25,512
This is almost intuitive.

26
00:01:25,592 --> 00:01:28,705
By default the mind
takes the apple as solid,

27
00:01:28,785 --> 00:01:31,463
out there, and undeniably objective.

28
00:01:31,543 --> 00:01:34,661
There on its own, whether
anyone looks or not.

29
00:01:35,482 --> 00:01:40,108
It feels solid, out there,
undeniably objective. But is it?

30
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:44,296
Pause here. Toss an apple,
or just picture one.

31
00:01:45,101 --> 00:01:50,890
Now ask: where exactly is this solid,
independent apple? Is it the red I see?

32
00:01:50,970 --> 00:01:54,545
The press on my palm? The
weight, the arc through the air?

33
00:01:54,625 --> 00:01:59,124
Is it any one of these, all of them
together, or something behind them?

34
00:01:59,204 --> 00:02:01,615
Look, and see what is actually found.

35
00:02:02,433 --> 00:02:05,546
Looked for, that solid apple is not found.

36
00:02:05,626 --> 00:02:08,358
What is there is many
appearings met together.

37
00:02:08,438 --> 00:02:12,855
Shapes and colours, the press on
the palm, the arc of the motion.

38
00:02:12,935 --> 00:02:16,048
They are gathered as one
apple by designation,

39
00:02:16,128 --> 00:02:19,246
so quick and smooth
that it goes unnoticed.

40
00:02:20,053 --> 00:02:22,568
And the apple works perfectly in the hand.

41
00:02:22,648 --> 00:02:25,068
It follows gravity and momentum.

42
00:02:25,148 --> 00:02:29,456
Yet it has no apple-ness inside
it, and no substrate under it.

43
00:02:29,536 --> 00:02:33,682
The shapes, the pressure and the
motion are not a bottom layer either.

44
00:02:33,762 --> 00:02:37,147
They are designated too,
and just as unfindable.

45
00:02:37,227 --> 00:02:38,981
So I am not catching a fiction.

46
00:02:39,061 --> 00:02:43,469
I am catching an apple that exists
only conventionally, and works.

47
00:02:44,273 --> 00:02:46,285
Let me go through the whole toss.

48
00:02:46,365 --> 00:02:51,027
I toss an apple to a friend, and my
friend catches it. Look at it twice.

49
00:02:51,107 --> 00:02:54,904
Once as the habit sees it, and
once as it actually occurs.

50
00:02:55,725 --> 00:02:59,666
As the habit sees it, a solid
apple flies through the air.

51
00:02:59,746 --> 00:03:04,028
It owns its shape, colour,
weight and smell as its own.

52
00:03:04,108 --> 00:03:07,723
A solid thrower sends it, and
a solid receiver takes it.

53
00:03:07,804 --> 00:03:12,669
I call this the inherent framework,
the matrix. It is not a thought I hold.

54
00:03:12,749 --> 00:03:15,821
It is a habit in the
body, before any thought,

55
00:03:15,901 --> 00:03:19,494
of taking what is singled out
as standing from its own side.

56
00:03:20,305 --> 00:03:22,168
Now look at the moment directly.

57
00:03:22,248 --> 00:03:26,189
No single apple-entity is
hiding behind the experience.

58
00:03:26,269 --> 00:03:29,301
There are many dependent
arisings, at once.

59
00:03:29,381 --> 00:03:32,942
The touch and the density,
where skin, nerve,

60
00:03:33,022 --> 00:03:35,293
pressure and resistance meet.

61
00:03:35,373 --> 00:03:40,048
The shape and the colour, where light,
eye and the angle of seeing meet.

62
00:03:40,128 --> 00:03:43,866
The scent, where what drifts
from the apple meets the nose.

63
00:03:43,946 --> 00:03:46,746
None of these belongs
to a hidden apple core.

64
00:03:46,826 --> 00:03:49,129
The conditions themselves
are the appearing.

65
00:03:49,962 --> 00:03:55,140
The apple is designated on a basis, as
a chariot is designated on its wheels,

66
00:03:55,220 --> 00:03:56,798
axle and frame.

67
00:03:56,878 --> 00:04:00,331
Its basis is the colour,
the shape, the touch,

68
00:04:00,411 --> 00:04:04,302
and what it is for: being
tossed, caught and eaten.

69
00:04:04,432 --> 00:04:08,170
"Apple" cuts experience into
a unit, so that I can toss it,

70
00:04:08,250 --> 00:04:10,005
catch it, or eat it.

71
00:04:10,085 --> 00:04:12,708
And if I look for the real
apple inside the parts,

72
00:04:12,788 --> 00:04:14,828
I find only more bases.

73
00:04:14,908 --> 00:04:19,950
Cells, molecules, tones of
colour, each designated in turn.

74
00:04:20,030 --> 00:04:22,455
No bottom brick is ever reached.

75
00:04:23,278 --> 00:04:25,141
Then why does the toss still work?

76
00:04:25,221 --> 00:04:30,291
Unfindable as a standalone object, the
apple still flies across the room and

77
00:04:30,371 --> 00:04:32,220
lands in my friend's hand.

78
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:35,576
This is causal efficacy
without causal power.

79
00:04:35,656 --> 00:04:40,073
When the conditions meet, the throwing,
the flight and the catching happen

80
00:04:40,153 --> 00:04:43,389
reliably. No apple-entity is needed.

81
00:04:43,469 --> 00:04:46,803
The meeting of conditions
is the working, completely.

82
00:04:47,618 --> 00:04:49,807
The thrower is singled out the same way.

83
00:04:49,887 --> 00:04:53,544
Anatta is first met as
no doer behind seeing:

84
00:04:53,624 --> 00:04:55,799
in the seen, just the seen.

85
00:04:55,879 --> 00:04:59,536
Dependent arising turns that
same seeing onto action.

86
00:04:59,616 --> 00:05:05,419
Intention arises, muscles contract,
momentum carries, the apple moves.

87
00:05:05,499 --> 00:05:09,114
No little me sits inside the
head, pulling the levers.

88
00:05:09,194 --> 00:05:12,457
The wind blows with no wind
apart from the blowing.

89
00:05:12,537 --> 00:05:15,858
The throwing happens with no
thrower standing behind it.

90
00:05:16,659 --> 00:05:20,193
Look for the hand, and
I find fingers, palm,

91
00:05:20,273 --> 00:05:22,639
bones, muscles and nerves.

92
00:05:22,719 --> 00:05:25,777
The person who throws is
designated on the body,

93
00:05:25,857 --> 00:05:29,147
sensations, intentions and movement.

94
00:05:29,227 --> 00:05:31,665
No ultimate thrower is reached.

95
00:05:31,795 --> 00:05:37,408
Thrower, apple, tossing and receiver
are designated together, as one event.

96
00:05:37,488 --> 00:05:38,893
None comes first.

97
00:05:39,706 --> 00:05:41,420
But nobody disappears.

98
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:46,121
The conventional person, the mere
I, is fully there to toss apples,

99
00:05:46,201 --> 00:05:48,829
keep promises, and catch the bus.

100
00:05:49,633 --> 00:05:51,401
And the toss tastes different.

101
00:05:51,481 --> 00:05:54,471
Centerless: no observer
sits at the middle.

102
00:05:54,551 --> 00:05:58,588
Effortless: no inner doer
grinds away to keep it going.

103
00:05:58,668 --> 00:06:02,732
Seamless and intimate: no
distance between thrower,

104
00:06:02,812 --> 00:06:05,939
apple and receiver. Yet nothing merges.

105
00:06:06,019 --> 00:06:09,584
The throw stays the throw,
and the catch stays the catch.

106
00:06:10,424 --> 00:06:13,156
For the same apple held
to the five elements,

107
00:06:13,236 --> 00:06:17,373
see my video on 5
Elements: Chinese vs Tibet.

108
00:06:18,190 --> 00:06:21,969
The second example is a
mountain. Does a mountain exist?

109
00:06:22,049 --> 00:06:23,722
The first answer is yes.

110
00:06:23,802 --> 00:06:27,241
It is a massive,
immovable fact of geology.

111
00:06:27,321 --> 00:06:29,469
But look for the mountain among the rocks,

112
00:06:29,549 --> 00:06:32,580
the soil, the height, the tree line.

113
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:35,637
It is not among them, and
it is not apart from them.

114
00:06:35,717 --> 00:06:39,636
It appears vividly, and it
reliably stops the climber,

115
00:06:39,739 --> 00:06:44,446
only in dependence on its conditions,
its parts and the name "mountain".

116
00:06:44,535 --> 00:06:46,466
This does not make it imaginary.

117
00:06:46,546 --> 00:06:48,640
It was there before anyone named it.

118
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:52,245
But no mountain comes with
its edges drawn by nature.

119
00:06:53,053 --> 00:06:56,152
Does a bat see a mountain? A bee? An ant?

120
00:06:56,232 --> 00:06:59,562
Ask each the same question,
is there a mountain there,

121
00:06:59,642 --> 00:07:03,901
and the answers will not match,
because the worlds do not match.

122
00:07:04,734 --> 00:07:08,296
I see a bounded shape against
the sky, with a summit,

123
00:07:08,376 --> 00:07:10,347
slopes and a base.

124
00:07:10,427 --> 00:07:15,103
A bat, finding its way by
echo, may meet returning sound,

125
00:07:15,183 --> 00:07:17,874
with no clean edge where mountain stops.

126
00:07:17,954 --> 00:07:21,950
A bee, seeing in ultraviolet
among flowers and light,

127
00:07:22,030 --> 00:07:25,089
may hardly meet the mountain
as one thing at all.

128
00:07:25,169 --> 00:07:27,752
An ant takes a day to cross one boulder.

129
00:07:27,832 --> 00:07:32,358
It meets ridges of grain, warmth
and the scent trails of its nest,

130
00:07:32,438 --> 00:07:33,803
and never a mountain.

131
00:07:34,618 --> 00:07:39,321
This is not four creatures looking at
one ready-made mountain from four angles.

132
00:07:39,401 --> 00:07:41,807
Body and world arise together.

133
00:07:41,887 --> 00:07:44,516
A different body singles
out a different world.

134
00:07:45,326 --> 00:07:49,282
The usual reply is that the
mountain is there all the same,

135
00:07:49,362 --> 00:07:51,605
and only the experiences differ.

136
00:07:51,685 --> 00:07:54,648
That reply slips in a noun, the mountain,

137
00:07:54,728 --> 00:07:58,317
finished before anything
meets it. That is the given.

138
00:07:58,397 --> 00:08:01,102
If the hidden mountain
has a summit and slopes,

139
00:08:01,182 --> 00:08:03,806
why do the bat and the
ant meet none of them?

140
00:08:03,886 --> 00:08:07,869
If it has no features at all, a
featureless something cannot be what they

141
00:08:07,949 --> 00:08:09,149
all meet.

142
00:08:09,773 --> 00:08:12,206
Nor is measuring a view from nowhere.

143
00:08:12,286 --> 00:08:16,935
Metres and maps are a human channel
of contact, as reliable as any.

144
00:08:17,015 --> 00:08:21,527
When we agree on where the mountain is, it
shows that our bodies and instruments are

145
00:08:21,607 --> 00:08:25,100
alike, like instruments
with the same calibration.

146
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:28,334
It does not show one mountain
standing there by itself.

147
00:08:28,414 --> 00:08:32,247
And the ant is not cut off:
a rockfall can crush it.

148
00:08:32,327 --> 00:08:36,527
So it is not one objective mountain
with many subjective pictures.

149
00:08:36,607 --> 00:08:40,983
The mountain, the one who meets it, and
the channel of meeting are designated

150
00:08:41,063 --> 00:08:44,439
together. None is the
bedrock under the others.

151
00:08:45,262 --> 00:08:47,872
When no one is looking,
is the mountain there?

152
00:08:47,952 --> 00:08:51,043
Two claims sound almost
the same, and are not.

153
00:08:51,186 --> 00:08:55,264
"The mountain is still there when
I look away and look back" is true.

154
00:08:55,344 --> 00:08:58,869
It is a conventional claim,
checked the ordinary way:

155
00:08:58,958 --> 00:09:03,434
looking again, others seeing it,
the road still there to drive on.

156
00:09:03,605 --> 00:09:08,565
"The mountain exists from its own side,
whether or not anything ever meets it" is

157
00:09:08,645 --> 00:09:11,188
a different claim. Nothing has earned it.

158
00:09:11,268 --> 00:09:14,720
It slips in because the first
claim works so reliably.

159
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:17,578
But reliability is not independence.

160
00:09:18,410 --> 00:09:20,889
That line keeps me out of two mistakes.

161
00:09:21,033 --> 00:09:24,635
"The mountain is an illusion",
which no one is claiming.

162
00:09:24,715 --> 00:09:28,606
And "the mountain exists on its
own", which was never shown.

163
00:09:29,430 --> 00:09:33,263
So, from the apple in the palm
to the mountain on the horizon,

164
00:09:33,343 --> 00:09:38,105
everything is unfindable, and
works perfectly all the same.

165
00:09:38,938 --> 00:09:41,684
I am not the first to say
it is not straightforward.

166
00:09:41,764 --> 00:09:46,467
In the Long Discourses, Ānanda tells
the Buddha how wonderful it is.

167
00:09:46,547 --> 00:09:51,902
Dependent arising is so deep, and yet
to him it seems as plain as can be.

168
00:09:51,982 --> 00:09:53,292
The Buddha stops him.

169
00:09:53,436 --> 00:09:55,298
"Do not say so, Ānanda.

170
00:09:55,378 --> 00:09:59,379
This dependent arising is
deep, and it appears deep."

171
00:09:59,482 --> 00:10:04,741
From not penetrating it, he says, this
generation is tangled like a knotted ball

172
00:10:04,821 --> 00:10:05,801
of thread.

173
00:10:05,881 --> 00:10:10,969
Ānanda was his closest attendant, and
he was told he had not yet understood.

174
00:10:11,785 --> 00:10:15,360
At this point, read my article
The Illusion of the Given.

175
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:18,512
The mountain is one case
of what it takes apart:

176
00:10:18,592 --> 00:10:21,202
the belief that one
world is already there,

177
00:10:21,282 --> 00:10:24,517
finished, and beings
only see it differently.

178
00:10:24,597 --> 00:10:26,650
It starts from one bowl of liquid.

179
00:10:26,730 --> 00:10:30,387
A human sees water, a
hungry ghost sees pus,

180
00:10:30,467 --> 00:10:35,323
a fish sees its home, and a god
sees nectar. Then come back here.

181
00:10:36,125 --> 00:10:39,387
Now the two words, as the
tradition defines them.

182
00:10:39,467 --> 00:10:44,129
Dependent arising is arising in
dependence on causes and conditions.

183
00:10:44,209 --> 00:10:47,268
Applied to suffering,
it is the twelve links,

184
00:10:47,348 --> 00:10:50,216
from ignorance to ageing and death.

185
00:10:50,296 --> 00:10:53,287
In forward order, how
suffering comes about.

186
00:10:53,367 --> 00:10:55,787
In reverse order, how it ends.

187
00:10:55,867 --> 00:10:59,238
Candrakīrti reads the
word itself: meeting,

188
00:10:59,318 --> 00:11:01,289
or depending, and arising.

189
00:11:01,369 --> 00:11:04,509
Madhyamaka widens it to every phenomenon.

190
00:11:04,589 --> 00:11:09,183
Nothing arises without depending,
so nothing has a nature of its own.

191
00:11:09,263 --> 00:11:12,784
Tsongkhapa sets out three
levels of dependence:

192
00:11:12,864 --> 00:11:18,617
on causes and conditions, on parts,
and, the subtlest, on designation.

193
00:11:19,425 --> 00:11:24,277
Designation is naming, by
word and concept, on a basis.

194
00:11:24,357 --> 00:11:27,347
The Abhidharma used it
to sort what exists.

195
00:11:27,427 --> 00:11:32,225
A chariot, a person, a forest
exist only as designated.

196
00:11:32,305 --> 00:11:36,043
The final units, they
said, exist substantially.

197
00:11:36,123 --> 00:11:38,448
Nāgārjuna takes that floor away.

198
00:11:38,528 --> 00:11:40,486
The units are designated too.

199
00:11:40,566 --> 00:11:46,206
In one verse he joins the two words:
what arises in dependence is emptiness,

200
00:11:46,286 --> 00:11:49,920
a designation in dependence,
and that is the middle way.

201
00:11:50,725 --> 00:11:53,906
Depending and being
designated are one fact,

202
00:11:53,986 --> 00:11:55,767
seen from two sides.

203
00:11:55,847 --> 00:12:00,006
And "by word and concept" does
not put the chariot in the mind.

204
00:12:00,086 --> 00:12:03,163
The concept that designates
is singled out too.

205
00:12:03,990 --> 00:12:05,677
I keep these definitions.

206
00:12:05,757 --> 00:12:09,739
One word needs care: "arising"
does not mean production.

207
00:12:09,819 --> 00:12:14,834
Conditions meet and this appears, and
nothing is born from its own side.

208
00:12:14,914 --> 00:12:19,318
In practice, these words
open into many key insights.

209
00:12:19,398 --> 00:12:23,883
They matter because we do not live
in the wisdom of dependent arising.

210
00:12:23,963 --> 00:12:29,209
If we did, every experience would
be vividly appearing yet unfindable.

211
00:12:29,289 --> 00:12:33,752
Centerless, mutual, seamless,
effortless and intimate.

212
00:12:34,557 --> 00:12:36,610
And it is stranger than it sounds.

213
00:12:36,690 --> 00:12:41,528
Nāgārjuna praises dependent
arising as free of eight extremes.

214
00:12:41,608 --> 00:12:46,488
No ceasing and no arising, no
annihilation and no permanence,

215
00:12:46,568 --> 00:12:51,053
no coming and no going, no
difference and no identity.

216
00:12:51,133 --> 00:12:56,438
What has no nature of its own cannot
really come from anywhere, or go anywhere.

217
00:12:57,241 --> 00:13:00,055
What arises in dependence appears vividly,

218
00:13:00,135 --> 00:13:01,767
yet is nowhere found.

219
00:13:01,847 --> 00:13:04,742
A rainbow appears with brilliant clarity,

220
00:13:04,822 --> 00:13:08,913
yet no rainbow-essence is found
in the droplets or the light.

221
00:13:08,993 --> 00:13:14,217
Vividness and unfindability are not
opposites. They are the same fact.

222
00:13:15,029 --> 00:13:17,598
Is long long in itself? No.

223
00:13:17,678 --> 00:13:23,173
It is long only beside short, and short
only beside long. They make each other.

224
00:13:23,985 --> 00:13:27,410
A subject is a subject only
with an object to know.

225
00:13:27,490 --> 00:13:30,603
Take away every object: where is the mind?

226
00:13:30,683 --> 00:13:33,524
Mind is a word for the
knowing side of appearing.

227
00:13:33,604 --> 00:13:38,909
It is as empty as what it knows, and it
is not the stuff everything is made of.

228
00:13:39,722 --> 00:13:41,544
Then what is cause and effect?

229
00:13:41,624 --> 00:13:46,273
We picture a force: A holds a
hidden power and pushes it into B.

230
00:13:46,353 --> 00:13:50,598
But A and B are not found, and
no power passes between them.

231
00:13:50,714 --> 00:13:53,188
Things come about in dependable patterns,

232
00:13:53,268 --> 00:13:56,218
and nothing standing by
itself enforces them.

233
00:13:56,298 --> 00:13:59,099
Causal efficacy without causal power.

234
00:13:59,179 --> 00:14:03,691
And because things are empty,
they can arise, change and work.

235
00:14:03,771 --> 00:14:06,042
That does not make emptiness a source.

236
00:14:06,122 --> 00:14:09,959
Being empty and arising in
dependence are one fact.

237
00:14:10,769 --> 00:14:13,827
All views and understanding
here are my own,

238
00:14:13,907 --> 00:14:16,259
from my practice and contemplation.

239
00:14:16,339 --> 00:14:20,340
I do not represent any
tradition, school or teacher.

240
00:14:21,141 --> 00:14:25,182
Next: what dependent arising
says. That is Part 2.

